<!doctype html>
<html amp lang="en">
{% include 'snippets/meta/amp-head.liquid' %}
  <body>
    <amp-sidebar id="sidebar" layout="nodisplay" side="left">
      <h5 class="right pad pointer" on="tap:sidebar.toggle" role="switch" tabindex="default">&lt;</h5>
      <div id="logoWrap" class="centerFlex">
        <svg id="logo" width="100" height="100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <polyline points="50,50 50,1 99,1 50,50 99,99 50,99 50,50 1,1 50,1" fill="black" stroke="lightskyblue" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="miter"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <nav class="navcolumn">
        <a href="index.html">profile</a>
        <a href="articles.html">articles</a>
        <a href="projects.html">projects</a>
      </nav>
    </amp-sidebar>

    <div class="site-shell">
      <div class="site-wrapper">
        {% include 'snippets/header/id-header.liquid' %}
        {% include 'snippets/header/page-header.liquid' %}

        <main class="main-content">
          <div class="card-grid">
            <article class="project-card">
              <div class="project-card__image preview-clip">
                <amp-img src="images/app-layout-465_project.png" alt="Polymer Elements App Layout"
                  srcset="images/app-layout-465_project.png 1024w, images/app-layout-354_project.png 768w, images/app-layout-240_project.png 320w"
                  width="100" height="100" layout="responsive"></amp-img>
              </div>
              <h3 class="project-card__title">Polymer Elements App Layout</h3>
              <p class="project-card__role">Contributions: May 2016</p>
              <div class="project-card__body">
                <p>App Layout is a collection of Polymer elements, along with guidelines and templates that can be used to structure your app’s layout. It's used by most Polymer progressive web apps.</p>
                <p>Early this year, I contributed a demo fix that improved the developer experience for app layout documentation.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="project-card__footer">
                <a href="https://polymerelements.github.io/app-layout/" class="button button--ghost" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View Project</a>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="project-card">
              <div class="project-card__image preview-clip">
                <amp-img src="images/static-search-465_project.png" alt="Ranked Static Search"
                  srcset="images/static-search-465_project.png 1024w, images/static-search-354_project.png 768w, images/static-search-240_project.png 320w"
                  width="100" height="100" layout="responsive"></amp-img>
              </div>
              <h3 class="project-card__title">Ranked Static Search (node.js)</h3>
              <p class="project-card__role">Created May 2015</p>
              <div class="project-card__body">
                <p>By indexing static content with this tool, ranked search results become possible on static sites. It creates a JSON object with TF-IDF scores that allows performant search using cosine similarity.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="project-card__footer">
                <a href="https://github.com/timBrockman/ranked-static-search" class="button button--ghost" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub</a>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="project-card">
              <div class="project-card__image preview-clip">
                <amp-img src="images/polymerfire-image-upload-465_project.png" alt="Firebase Image Upload"
                  srcset="images/polymerfire-image-upload-465_project.png 1024w, images/polymerfire-image-upload-354_project.png 768w, images/polymerfire-image-upload-240_project.png 320w"
                  width="100" height="100" layout="responsive"></amp-img>
              </div>
              <h3 class="project-card__title">Firebase Image Upload</h3>
              <p class="project-card__role">Created July 2016</p>
              <div class="project-card__body">
                <p>Firebase Image Upload is a simple Polymer element using PolymerFire to upload images (or files) to Firebase Storage. It demonstrates a lightweight file upload flow for Polymer apps.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="project-card__footer">
                <a href="https://github.com/timBrockman/firebase-image-upload" class="button button--ghost" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub</a>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="project-card">
              <div class="project-card__image preview-clip">
                <amp-img src="images/k8s-465_project.png" alt="Kubernetes Contribution"
                  srcset="images/k8s-465_project.png 1024w, images/k8s-354_project.png 768w, images/k8s-240_project.png 320w"
                  width="100" height="100" layout="responsive"></amp-img>
              </div>
              <h3 class="project-card__title">Kubernetes (k8s.io)</h3>
              <p class="project-card__role">Contributions: May - June 2016</p>
              <div class="project-card__body">
                <p>I improved Kubernetes documentation for Docker port handling on macOS, helping new developers trust the onboarding experience.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="project-card__footer">
                <a href="https://kubernetes.io" class="button button--ghost" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View Project</a>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </main>

        {% include 'snippets/footer/footer.liquid' %}
      </div>
    </div>

  {% include 'snippets/body/analytics.liquid' %}
  </body>
</html>
